---
import { weightStorage, servingTimeline, plannedRoute, seededTraining, roofline, type Point } from '../data/program-labs';
import { discovery } from '../data/program-discovery';
interface Props { kind: keyof typeof discovery; }
const { kind } = Astro.props;
const weights = [32,16,8,4].map(bits => ({ bits, ...weightStorage(7,bits) }));
const timeline = servingTimeline(false);
const route = plannedRoute();
const training = seededTraining();
const points = training.returns.map((value, i) => `${40 + i * 5.8},${160 - value * .6}`).join(' ');
---
<section class="calculated-chart" data-lab={kind} aria-label="Teaching experiment">
  {kind === 'agents' && <><h3>Evidence and permission are separate checks.</h3><p>Fictional policy §1: “A manager must review remote-work requests.” Preparation: approved document → passages → index. Request-time retrieval only reads permitted passages.</p><div class="scenario-buttons"><button type="button" data-scenario="evidence" aria-pressed="true">Evidence available</button><button type="button" data-scenario="missing" aria-pressed="false">Missing evidence</button><button type="button" data-scenario="denied" aria-pressed="false">Denied action</button></div><p class="scenario-output" aria-live="polite">The assistant can cite §1 and prepare a draft. Submission requires a separate permitted tool and human review.</p><p class="chart-note">Authored local demonstration; no model call, training or external action.</p></>}
  {kind === 'infrastructure' && <><h3>How much storage do the model weights need?</h3><label>Parameter count<select data-parameters><option value="1">1 billion</option><option value="7" selected>7 billion</option><option value="13">13 billion</option><option value="70">70 billion</option></select></label><p class="chart-note">Calculated: parameters × bits per parameter ÷ 8. GB = 10⁹ bytes; GiB = 2³⁰ bytes. Uniform precision and ideal packed storage.</p><div data-weight-bars>{weights.map(w => <div><span>{w.bits}-bit: <span data-weight-value={w.bits}>{w.gb.toFixed(2)} GB / {w.gib.toFixed(2)} GiB</span></span><div class="chart-bar"><span data-weight-bar={w.bits} style={`width:${w.gb/28*100}%`}></span></div></div>)}</div><label>Inspect one precision<select data-bits><option value="32">32-bit</option><option value="16" selected>16-bit</option><option value="8">8-bit</option><option value="4">4-bit packed</option></select></label><output class="chart-output" aria-live="polite" data-weight-output>7 billion × 16 bits ÷ 8 = 14.00 GB / 13.04 GiB.</output><p class="chart-note">Weight storage only. Excludes runtime memory, key-value cache, activations, gradients, optimizer states and quantization metadata. This does not establish whether a model fits on a GPU.</p></>}
  {kind === 'performance' && <><h3>When does batching add waiting?</h3><p class="chart-note">SIMULATION. Four requests arrive at 0, 1, 2, 3 ms. One worker. Setup takes 4 ms per batch; each request adds 1 ms. A batch of four starts at 3 ms, finishes at 11 ms, and returns all outputs together. No overlap, variable lengths or GPU measurements.</p><div class="scenario-buttons"><button type="button" data-policy="individual" aria-pressed="true">Individual</button><button type="button" data-policy="batch" aria-pressed="false">Batch of four</button></div><div data-timeline>{timeline.requests.map(r => <div class="request-row"><span>Request {r.id}</span><div class="request-track" aria-label={`Arrives ${r.arrival} ms, waits ${r.wait} ms, processes ${r.finish-r.start} ms, completes ${r.finish} ms`}><span class="request-wait" style={`left:${r.arrival/20*100}%;width:${r.wait/20*100}%`}></span><span class="request-compute" style={`left:${r.start/20*100}%;width:${(r.finish-r.start)/20*100}%`}></span></div></div>)}</div><div class="timeline-axis"><span>0</span><span>5</span><span>10</span><span>15</span><span>20 ms</span></div><p class="chart-note">Amber = waiting; violet = processing. The text alternative includes each duration.</p><output class="chart-output" data-timeline-output aria-live="polite">Individual: 200 requests/s; mean latency 11.00 ms; first response 5 ms. Calculated from this finite workload.</output></>}
  {kind === 'robotics' && <><h3>A map is an estimate of the environment.</h3><p>Prepared 4 × 4 grid. A breadth-first search finds a shortest route using four-direction moves. Coordinates are grid cells, not metres. A simulated robot stops if its next cell is occupied.</p><div class="scenario-buttons"><button type="button" data-map="known" aria-pressed="true">Known obstacles</button><button type="button" data-map="moved" aria-pressed="false">Move an obstacle</button><button type="button" data-map="missing" aria-pressed="false">Incomplete map</button></div><svg class="map-svg" viewBox="0 0 300 300" role="img" aria-label="Planned and simulated route on a four by four grid"><g>{Array.from({length:16},(_,i)=><rect x={40+(i%4)*55} y={205-Math.floor(i/4)*55} width="50" height="50" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" opacity=".25"/>)}</g><g data-obstacles>{[[1,1],[2,1],[1,3]].map(([x,y])=><rect x={40+x*55} y={205-y*55} width="50" height="50" fill="#d97706"/>)}</g><polyline data-route points={route.map(([x,y])=>`${65+x*55},${230-y*55}`).join(' ')} stroke="#7c3aed" stroke-width="6" stroke-dasharray="8 4" fill="none"/><polyline data-actual points={route.map(([x,y])=>`${65+x*55},${230-y*55}`).join(' ')} stroke="#0d9488" stroke-width="3" fill="none"/>{[0,1,2,3].map(i=><><text x={65+i*55} y="275" fill="currentColor" font-size="12">{i}</text><text x="20" y={234-i*55} fill="currentColor" font-size="12">{i}</text></>)}<text x="145" y="295" fill="currentColor" font-size="12">x (cells)</text><text x="5" y="15" fill="currentColor" font-size="12">y (cells)</text></svg><p class="scenario-output" aria-live="polite">Known map: planned route and simulated trajectory reach (3,3) from (0,0). Violet dashes = plan; teal line = simulated trajectory.</p><p class="chart-note">This discrete simulation omits inertia, sensing uncertainty and stopping distance. It does not demonstrate real-world safety.</p></>}
  {kind === 'research' && <><h3>What did the training actually record?</h3><p class="chart-note">Local tabular Q-learning, 4 × 4 grid, seed 17, 80 episodes, up to 40 steps each. Learning rate 0.5; discount 0.9; exploration probability 0.25. Reward: −1 per move, −4 extra for collision, +20 extra at the goal. Terminal goal has no bootstrapped value.</p><svg class="map-svg" viewBox="0 0 540 310" role="img" aria-label="Recorded episode returns from seeded Q-learning; values fluctuate"><path d="M40 30V270H515" stroke="currentColor" fill="none"/>{[-160,-80,0,20].map(v=><text x="4" y={164-v*.6} font-size="11" fill="currentColor">{v}</text>)}<polyline points={points} fill="none" stroke="#7c3aed" stroke-width="2"/><text x="45" y="290" fill="currentColor" font-size="12">1</text><text x="490" y="290" fill="currentColor" font-size="12">80</text><text x="230" y="305" fill="currentColor" font-size="12">Episode</text><text x="45" y="20" fill="currentColor" font-size="12">Return (reward units)</text></svg><details><summary>Read all recorded returns</summary><p>{training.returns.map((r,i)=>`${i+1}: ${r}`).join('; ')}</p></details><p>The graph is generated by the same seeded learning model in the source. Its exploration decisions can make later episodes worse; a smooth rising curve would hide that behavior.</p><div class="scenario-buttons"><button type="button" data-reward="goal" aria-pressed="true">Reward reaching the goal</button><button type="button" data-reward="steps" aria-pressed="false">Reward every step</button></div><p class="scenario-output" aria-live="polite">With −1 per move and +20 at the goal, a six-move route returns 14. Finishing sooner avoids extra movement penalties.</p></>}
  {kind === 'cloud' && <><h3>Identity does not grant every permission.</h3><p>Fictional application policy: the employee role may read procedures, but only the publisher role may update them. The application gateway authenticates the token; a separate authorization middleware evaluates role and requested operation before service routing.</p><div class="scenario-buttons"><button type="button" data-access="read" aria-pressed="true">Employee reads</button><button type="button" data-access="write" aria-pressed="false">Employee writes</button><button type="button" data-access="anonymous" aria-pressed="false">Missing identity</button></div><p class="scenario-output" aria-live="polite">Authenticated employee, GET procedures: policy allows the read. Route to procedure service → model context → answer; observability records the decision.</p><p class="chart-note">Application authorization is separate from Kubernetes API authorization. Network boundaries and locks in the artwork do not prove security or compliance.</p></>}
  {kind === 'hardware' && <><h3>Which ceiling limits this hypothetical workload?</h3><p class="chart-note">Calculated Roofline ceiling: min(peak compute, bandwidth × operational intensity). Authored device assumptions: 100 GFLOP/s compute and 10 GB/s memory bandwidth. Operational intensity counts FLOPs per byte transferred from the specified external memory. No measured performance.</p><svg class="map-svg" viewBox="0 0 540 310" role="img" aria-label="Hypothetical Roofline: linear bandwidth ceiling until 10 FLOP per byte, then compute ceiling 100 GFLOP per second"><path d="M50 30V260H510" stroke="currentColor" fill="none"/><polyline points={[0,2,4,6,8,10,16,24,32].map(i=>`${50+i/32*450},${260-roofline(i)/100*210}`).join(' ')} fill="none" stroke="#7c3aed" stroke-width="4"/>{[0,8,16,24,32].map(i=><text x={50+i/32*450} y="280" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" fill="currentColor">{i}</text>)}<text x="8" y="55" fill="currentColor" font-size="12">100</text><text x="22" y="260" fill="currentColor" font-size="12">0</text><text x="55" y="18" fill="currentColor" font-size="12">Ceiling (GFLOP/s)</text><text x="160" y="305" fill="currentColor" font-size="12">Operational intensity (FLOP/byte)</text></svg><label>Inspect operational intensity<select data-intensity>{[1,4,8,10,16,32].map(i=><option value={i} selected={i===4}>{i} FLOP/byte</option>)}</select></label><output class="chart-output" data-roof-output aria-live="polite">4 FLOP/byte × 10 GB/s = 40 GFLOP/s ceiling; limited by data movement.</output><p class="chart-note">Real performance can be below either ceiling. Cache reuse, precision, access pattern and synchronization change the model inputs. FLOP means floating-point operation.</p></>}
  {kind === 'leadership' && <><h3>Compare ownership before choosing a platform.</h3><label>Which constraint matters most?<select data-constraint><option value="autonomy">Team autonomy</option><option value="residency">Data residency</option><option value="integration">Integration complexity</option></select></label><table class="architecture-matrix"><caption>Hypothetical alternatives, not measured rankings</caption><thead><tr><th>Decision</th><th>Shared platform</th><th>Team-owned systems</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>Ownership</th><td>Platform team owns shared service; application teams own use cases.</td><td>Each team owns its service, releases and incident response.</td></tr><tr><th>Integration</th><td>Common contract; changes require cross-team coordination.</td><td>Independent contracts; duplicated integration work is possible.</td></tr><tr><th>Data boundary</th><td>Requires scoped access and permitted deployment regions.</td><td>Local boundaries can simplify isolation but still need governance.</td></tr></tbody></table><p class="scenario-output" aria-live="polite">Team autonomy: examine the application teams’ release dependencies and support ownership. Neither design removes the need for a shared data contract.</p><p class="chart-note">Record context, decision, alternatives, consequences and a review trigger. No readiness score or unsupported cost advantage.</p></>}
  {kind === 'deployment' && <><h3>Follow a customer-delivery example.</h3><p>Fictional operations team cannot find current internal procedures. The acceptance check is agreed before implementing a search prototype.</p><label>Inspect a delivery stage<select data-delivery><option value="0">1 · Problem statement</option><option value="1">2 · Data assessment</option><option value="2">3 · Acceptance criteria</option><option value="3">4 · Prototype</option><option value="4">5 · Deployment plan</option><option value="5">6 · Validation report</option></select></label><div class="scenario-buttons"><button type="button" data-finding="available" aria-pressed="true">Approved data available</button><button type="button" data-finding="missing" aria-pressed="false">Procedures are incomplete</button></div><p class="scenario-output" aria-live="polite">Problem statement: procedure lookup is difficult. Confirm which users need which documents and how a useful answer will be checked.</p><p class="chart-note">No real client outcome or time-saving claim. Feedback can change the problem scope, not just tune a model.</p></>}
</section>
<script>
  import { mountProgramLabs } from '../scripts/program-labs';
  mountProgramLabs();
</script>
